The offline history catalog contains reviewed class metadata derived from public
Android SDK signatures at platform/prebuilts/sdk commit
3af7c93524be6f51e092b87b17f009f13ee98b43. Complete SDK binaries and signature files
are not bundled in the app. The original repository NOTICE is retained as
licenses/android-sdk-NOTICE.txt. It contains SDK terms, not an Apache declaration.

The historical resource exporter analyzes Android Open Source Project framework
sources. The reviewed KitKat framework commit is
63ade05d76785975fc3292ca030abbaa1dda8891. Its root module declares Apache 2.0.
The original root NOTICE is retained as licenses/aosp-frameworks-base-NOTICE.txt,
including its additional third-party attributions. The full Apache 2.0 license
is in licenses/Apache-2.0.txt. Framework resource exports include notices from
their actual release commits; the bundled KitKat notice does not replace those.

Selected original AOSP bitmap and nine-patch resources, adapted drawable XML,
and release color bindings are bundled for Classic, Holo, and Material Design 1
control recreations. The immutable commits, complete source and bundled hashes,
and adaptations are in the app asset aosp-resources/controls.json. Original
ancestor notices are retained under licenses/aosp-resources and collected in
licenses/aosp-resources-NOTICE.txt. XML resource names and private references
are adapted for the app namespace; text has a 16sp readability floor.

Toast recreations additionally use AOSP layouts and backgrounds from Android
2.3.7, 4.4.4, 5.0.2, 9, 12, and 16. Their original layout text, immutable source
URLs, source and bundled hashes, and explicit adaptations are retained in
aosp-resources/toasts.json. Hashes describe resource bytes before Android
resource compilation. The popup belongs to Componentory and does not invoke
the installed OS Toast renderer. Modern colors follow the selected library
palette; historical resource reuse does not imply a Compose Toast API.

These resource recreations still use the installed OS interaction engine.
Other platform samples use current-OS widgets with the chosen theme. Library
samples use the explicitly recorded Compose Material library versions. No
original historical OS captures are bundled. Resource reuse does not establish
original historical OS behavior.

Original notice URLs, immutable commits, and byte hashes are in
licenses/provenance.json. These attribution files do not change upstream terms
or assign a single license to every AOSP or SDK file.

The inline-content demo uses androidx.autofill:autofill:1.3.0 to construct the
inline UI v1 template. This AndroidX module is licensed under Apache 2.0. Its
original published license is retained as licenses/androidx-autofill-LICENSE.txt,
with its artifact identity and byte hashes in licenses/provenance.json. The
InlineContentView itself is created by the installed Android platform.

